  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a group of Buddhist monks in orange robes standing in a park-like setting. The overlaid text reads, \"how dare people make fun of our peaceful religion.\" The meme's intent is to portray Buddhism as a peaceful, sacred, and sacredly protected religion, implying that any mockery of it is an affront or an act of disrespect. This framing is inherently hateful as it targets a specific religious group (Buddhists) by invoking a sense of offense and moral outrage, suggesting that criticism of their beliefs or practices is unacceptable or even blasphemous. The meme uses the visual of the monks to symbolize the religion's perceived innocence and peace, and the text to frame any criticism as a violation of that peace, thus creating a hostile and defensive tone that attacks those who might question or mock the religion. This is a form of religious intolerance and can be seen as a hate-based response to criticism, aiming to delegitimize dissent by labeling it as an attack on a sacred institution.",
